  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🪓 Nord Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Old Norse first names, Battle-Born-style family names and epithets for the Nords of Skyrim."
    },
    "intro": "Nords are named like the <a href=\"viking-name-generator.html\">Vikings</a> they're based on. Skyrim is full of Old Norse-sounding first names (Ulfric, Ralof, Hadvar), proud hyphenated family names like the Battle-Borns and Gray-Manes of Whiterun, and <a href=\"epithet-generator.html\">epithets</a> like Balgruuf the Greater and Elisif the Fair. This **Nord name generator** builds all three, for Skyrim, Elder Scrolls Online or your own saga.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Three kinds of Nord name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>A family name, hyphenated.</strong> Skyrim's great families have two-part names: the Battle-Borns and Gray-Manes feuding in Whiterun, the Black-Briars in Riften, the Silver-Bloods in Markarth and the Shatter-Shields in Windhelm. Each half is a plain, strong word.</li><li><strong>An epithet.</strong> Rulers and heroes are often known by a title: Jarl Balgruuf the Greater, Jarl Elisif the Fair, Aela the Huntress.</li><li><strong>A single name.</strong> Plenty of Nords go by one name, like Ralof and Hadvar from Skyrim's opening.</li></ul><p>The generator's family names are new combinations, built from the same kind of words, so your Nord won't belong to one of the game's families (unless you get very lucky).</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Why Nord names sound Norse",
        "content": "<p>The Nords came to Skyrim from Atmora, a cold continent to the north, led in legend by Ysgramor. Bethesda modelled them on the Norse, and the first names show it: many are real Old Norse names or close to them.</p><p>The first names in this generator are real Old Norse names, the kind found in the Icelandic sagas: Gunnar, Njal and Egil for men, Astrid, Gudrun and Freydis for women. They fit Skyrim because Skyrim was built to sound like them.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Choosing a name for your Dragonborn",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Single name or family?</strong> A Nord from a great family carries its feuds. A Nord with one name can make their own.</li><li><strong>Let the epithet be earned.</strong> Start as Sigrid, end the game as Sigrid Storm-Caller.</li><li><strong>Say it like a shout.</strong> Nord names are short and strong, which suits a people who settle arguments with the Thu'um.</li></ul><p>For other races of Tamriel, try the <a href=\"khajiit-name-generator.html\">Khajiit</a> and <a href=\"skyrim-orc-name-generator.html\">Skyrim Orc</a> name generators.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do Nord last names work in Skyrim?",
        "answer": "The great families have hyphenated names made of two strong words, like Battle-Born, Gray-Mane and Black-Briar. Many Nords have no family name at all, and rulers often use an epithet instead, like Balgruuf the Greater."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are Nord names based on real names?",
        "answer": "Yes, many are Old Norse or close to it. The first names in this generator are real Old Norse names from the sagas."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use these names in Elder Scrolls Online?",
        "answer": "Yes. ESO names must be unique on your server, and a hyphenated family name or an epithet makes it easier to find one that's free."
      }
    ]
  }
